page DocsProviderDomains

title "Domains - Documentation"

template
<div class="min-h-[calc(100vh-4rem)] grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] bg-page transition-colors">

  <DocsSidebar active="provider-domains" />

  <div class="min-w-0 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-10 py-6 sm:py-10">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">

    <article class="rounded-3xl border border-line bg-panel p-5 sm:p-8">
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Documentation / Cloud providers</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-light uppercase tracking-wide text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">Domains</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-sm mt-2 mb-8">DNS zones hosted at the provider.</p>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">The list</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Each row shows the domain and how many DNS records it has. Type in the search box to filter. <strong>DNS records</strong> opens the <a href="/docs/providers/dns-records" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">records page</a>.</p>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Add a domain</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Select <strong>Add domain</strong> and type the domain, such as example.com. On Linode you also give an SOA email, the contact address for the zone. Select Create domain.</p>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border-l-2 border-l-brand-500 bg-brand-500/5 px-4 py-3 mb-8">
        <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">Creating the zone is not enough. In your registrar, point the domain's nameservers at the provider. Until you do, the records here are not used.</p>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Delete a domain</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">Select <strong>Delete</strong>, then <strong>Yes, delete</strong>. With two-factor sign-in on, you must enter a code first: a code from your authenticator app or a recovery code, or select <strong>Text me a code</strong> if you use SMS. Deleting removes the zone and all its records at the provider.</p>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">If something goes wrong</h2>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-8">
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't create the domain. Try again.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Check the domain name and, on Linode, the SOA email.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Enter a verification code to delete this domain.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Two-factor is on. Enter a fresh code and select Yes, delete again.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't delete that domain.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Read the message under the page title.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">If the API token is missing a permission this page needs, a message at the top says which one and how to fix it. Add the permission to the token at the provider, then reload.</p>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-8 pt-5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
        <a href="/docs/providers/ips" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">&larr; IP addresses</a>
        <a href="/docs/providers/dns-records" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">DNS records &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

  </div>
  </div>
</div>
